<section class="full" aria-label="What’s inside">
  <h2 class="section-title">What’s inside the Metrics Dictionary</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Metric ID + Group:</strong> stable identifier and domain grouping for navigation and change control.</li>
    <li><strong>Definition + Interpretation:</strong> what it means and what movement usually implies.</li>
    <li><strong>Formula + inputs:</strong> explicit numerator/denominator and calculation logic.</li>
    <li><strong>Grain + filters:</strong> what level the metric is valid at (candidate, req, employee, day/week) and which filters apply.</li>
    <li><strong>Data mapping:</strong> where the metric lives (object/field) and which system is the source of truth.</li>
    <li><strong>Governance:</strong> owner, refresh cadence, and target (when applicable).</li>
  </ul>
</section>

